-- Companion file for the tutorial "When a Rule Cannot Answer".
--
-- The page's subject is Regulation Crowdfunding, part 227 of title 17 of the
-- Code of Federal Regulations, which commenced on 2016-05-16. This file holds
-- every example the page shows that runs today: the recap, the careless
-- encoding of Step 1, the refusal that repairs it in Step 2, the screens of
-- Step 3, the look-alikes of Steps 4 and 5, the uncatchability of Step 6, the
-- ordering of Step 7 and the tests of Step 8.
--
--     l4 run when-a-rule-cannot-answer.l4

IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate

§ `0. What a rule is`

-- A rule is told some facts about the case in front of it -- its inputs, the
-- names listed after GIVEN -- and works out one answer, its output, whose kind
-- of thing is named after GIVETH. This one is told a person and answers
-- yes-or-no. Alex is 17, so the answer is FALSE.

DECLARE Person
    HAS name IS A STRING
        age IS A NUMBER

GIVEN alex IS A Person
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`is over 18` alex MEANS alex's age AT LEAST 18

`Alex, aged 17` MEANS Person WITH name IS "Alex", age IS 17

#EVAL `is over 18` `Alex, aged 17`   -- FALSE

§ `1. A confident wrong answer`

-- The offering limit has had three regimes. Encoded with no floor under the
-- oldest arm, the commencement-day figure is handed out for every date before
-- commencement as well -- including dates on which part 227 did not exist.

@ref 17 CFR 227.100(a)(1) — the offering maximum, encoded without a floor
GIVEN `rule date` IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
`unfloored offering maximum` MEANS
    BRANCH
       IF `rule date` AT LEAST Date 15 3 2021 THEN 5000000
       IF `rule date` AT LEAST Date 12 4 2017 THEN 1070000
       OTHERWISE 1000000

#EVAL `unfloored offering maximum` (Date 1 6 2016)   -- 1000000, correct
#EVAL `unfloored offering maximum` (Date 1 1 2016)   -- 1000000, and wrong

§ `2. The refusal, and the rule that uses it`

-- One named definition per refusal; the name is the message; an @ref above it
-- says why the encoding stops here; every rule that needs it uses the name.

@ref 80 FR 71388 (Rel. 33-9974) — 17 CFR part 227 commences on 2016-05-16
GIVETH A NUMBER
`no Regulation Crowdfunding figure exists before commencement on 2016-05-16` MEANS
    REFUSE "no Regulation Crowdfunding figure exists before commencement on 2016-05-16"

@ref 17 CFR 227.100(a)(1) — offering maximum in a 12-month period
GIVEN `rule date` IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
`offering maximum in a 12-month period` MEANS
    BRANCH
       IF `rule date` AT LEAST Date 15 3 2021 THEN 5000000
       IF `rule date` AT LEAST Date 12 4 2017 THEN 1070000
       IF `rule date` AT LEAST Date 16 5 2016 THEN 1000000
       OTHERWISE `no Regulation Crowdfunding figure exists before commencement on 2016-05-16`

#EVAL `offering maximum in a 12-month period` (Date 1 6 2016)   -- 1000000
#EVAL `offering maximum in a 12-month period` (Date 1 1 2016)   -- refused

#ASSERT REFUSED (`offering maximum in a 12-month period` (Date 1 1 2016))
#ASSERT REFUSED (`offering maximum in a 12-month period` (Date 1 1 2016)) BECAUSE "no Regulation Crowdfunding figure exists before commencement on 2016-05-16"

§ `3. The law does not apply: a value, not a refusal`

-- "Was it in force?" has an answer on every date there has ever been. It is
-- determinate, so it is an ordinary value that other rules can read.

@ref 80 FR 71388 (Rel. 33-9974) — part 227 is in force from 2016-05-16
GIVEN `rule date` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Regulation Crowdfunding is in force on` `rule date` MEANS
    `rule date` AT LEAST Date 16 5 2016

#ASSERT NOT (`Regulation Crowdfunding is in force on` (Date 1 1 2016))
#ASSERT `Regulation Crowdfunding is in force on` (Date 1 6 2016)

-- The same shape carries a savings provision. This licensing regime is
-- invented, to keep the example short: it is repealed on 2024-01-01, and an
-- application filed before the repeal is still decided under the old Act,
-- because the law says so. That rule is a rule, and it answers.

DECLARE Application
    HAS `filed on` IS A DATE

GIVETH A DATE
`the repeal took effect` MEANS Date 1 1 2024

GIVEN application IS AN Application
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`is decided under the old Act` application MEANS
    NOT (application's `filed on` AT LEAST `the repeal took effect`)

`the November application` MEANS Application WITH `filed on` IS Date 3 11 2023

#ASSERT `is decided under the old Act` `the November application`

§ `4. A value that may be absent`

-- A first-time issuer has raised nothing in the previous 12 months. The
-- absence is a fact about that issuer, and the rule knows what to do with it.

DECLARE Issuer
    HAS name IS A STRING
        `amount raised in the previous 12 months` IS A MAYBE NUMBER

GIVEN issuer IS AN Issuer
GIVETH A NUMBER
`prior raises counted against the limit` issuer MEANS
    CONSIDER issuer's `amount raised in the previous 12 months`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN 0
    WHEN JUST amount THEN amount

`Foundry Labs, a first-time issuer` MEANS Issuer WITH name IS "Foundry Labs", `amount raised in the previous 12 months` IS NOTHING
`Ellsworth Tools, a returning issuer` MEANS Issuer WITH name IS "Ellsworth Tools", `amount raised in the previous 12 months` IS JUST 400000

#EVAL `prior raises counted against the limit` `Foundry Labs, a first-time issuer`     -- 0
#EVAL `prior raises counted against the limit` `Ellsworth Tools, a returning issuer`   -- 400000

§ `5. A failure with a reason`

-- A rejected filing is not the absence of an answer. It is an answer, and it
-- carries the ground of rejection, which the rule that relies on it reads and
-- acts on.

DECLARE `Form C filing`
    HAS `has the required financial statements` IS A BOOLEAN
        `is signed` IS A BOOLEAN

@ref 17 CFR 227.203 — the offering statement and its required contents
GIVEN filing IS A `Form C filing`
GIVETH AN EITHER STRING BOOLEAN
`the filing is accepted` filing MEANS
    BRANCH
       IF NOT filing's `has the required financial statements`
           THEN LEFT "rejected: the required financial statements are missing"
       IF NOT filing's `is signed`
           THEN LEFT "rejected: the filing is not signed"
       OTHERWISE RIGHT TRUE

GIVEN filing IS A `Form C filing`
GIVETH A STRING
`what the intermediary tells the issuer` filing MEANS
    CONSIDER `the filing is accepted` filing
    WHEN LEFT reason THEN reason
    WHEN RIGHT accepted THEN "accepted"

`Foundry Labs' unsigned filing` MEANS `Form C filing` WITH `has the required financial statements` IS TRUE, `is signed` IS FALSE

#EVAL `what the intermediary tells the issuer` `Foundry Labs' unsigned filing`

§ `6. Nothing downstream can turn a refusal into an answer`

-- Wrapping the refusal in a MAYBE and defaulting the absent case does not
-- soften it: to choose an arm, CONSIDER has to look, and looking is what
-- refuses. The refusal reaches the boundary unchanged.

GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`the figure, if the model has one` MEANS
    JUST `no Regulation Crowdfunding figure exists before commencement on 2016-05-16`

GIVETH A NUMBER
`an attempt to default the refusal` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the figure, if the model has one`
    WHEN JUST amount THEN amount
    WHEN NOTHING THEN 0

#EVAL `an attempt to default the refusal`
#ASSERT REFUSED `an attempt to default the refusal` BECAUSE "no Regulation Crowdfunding figure exists before commencement on 2016-05-16"

§ `7. Order matters, a little`

@ref 17 CFR 227.100(b)(1) — foreign private issuers are outside part 227
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the model does not cover offerings by foreign private issuers` MEANS
    REFUSE "the model does not cover offerings by foreign private issuers"

#ASSERT NOT (FALSE AND `the model does not cover offerings by foreign private issuers`)
#ASSERT REFUSED (`the model does not cover offerings by foreign private issuers` AND FALSE)

§ `8. The drafting placeholder`

-- TBD comes from the prelude. It is a refusal that says the rule has not been
-- written yet, so a half-finished file gives an honest non-answer instead of a
-- placeholder TRUE someone later mistakes for a conclusion.

@ref 17 CFR 227.202 — ongoing reporting requirements, not yet encoded
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the issuer's ongoing reporting obligations are satisfied` MEANS TBD

-- The message a TBD carries is the prelude's own, not one this file wrote:
--   TBD: this rule has not been written yet
#EVAL `the issuer's ongoing reporting obligations are satisfied`
#ASSERT REFUSED `the issuer's ongoing reporting obligations are satisfied`
